nodes.body:
@rkarhila-amd Thanks for the review. Both points:

1. **TP4:** agreed, and done in `6fc61acf80`. At two ranks every all-reduce implementation is batch-invariant, at four or more RCCL, the two-stage and AITER all-reduces are not, so TP4 covers more. On MI350X in the AMD CI environment the TP4 test passes 5 of 5 runs with #34543 and catches the bug without it in 6 of 8 (TP2: 3 of 4).
2. **TP1 test:** I'd keep it. `test_deterministic.py` is shared with CUDA (FlashInfer, FA3) and XPU, runs per PR on MI300 (`stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd`), and also covers `single` mode; the TP4 test runs only on the MI35x 8-GPU stage-c suite and checks only prefix log-probabilities. Removing it would drop per-PR deterministic coverage on MI300.

